From: NanoKVM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: park the CPU while its PLL is retuned

The CV18xx CPU mux can only divide whatever its parent PLL produces, so
reaching a frequency the firmware did not configure means changing MPLL
itself. Retuning a PLL that a CPU is executing from hangs that CPU: the
SG200X TRM requires every consumer to move to another stable clock first.

The common clock framework cannot express that ordering, so watch the PLL
instead. On PRE_RATE_CHANGE park the CPU on the mux's other lane, which
runs from its own untouched PLL at no more than either endpoint. On
POST_RATE_CHANGE return to it, but only after the hardware reports a
completed update and a real lock.

Two clk_change_rate() properties make the obvious implementation wrong.
It discards set_rate() errors, so the PLL's own return value never
reaches the caller; and it skips POST_RATE_CHANGE when the recalculated
rate is unchanged, so a PLL that rejected the new rate outright would
strand the CPU on the alternate lane forever. mmux_set_rate() therefore
runs unconditionally afterwards and releases a mux that is still parked.

A PLL that was rewritten but never locked is the one case where the CPU
deliberately stays on the alternate lane. That is slower than requested,
but it is running, and recalc_rate() reports the truth.

The same park/unpark pair replaces the open-coded inactive-lane sequence
used for divider-only changes, which did the identical thing inline. The
selector register is now read-modify-written rather than restored
wholesale, because the two halves of a transition no longer share one
critical section and neighbouring clocks own the other bits.

Also propagate fpll_find_rate() failures, which the integer path already
reports, and add a lock poll a parked consumer can use to ask whether
returning to its PLL is safe.

This adds no operating point by itself: a board still has to ask for a
different MPLL rate, and no core supply voltage is changed.

References:
  SG200X TRM, "PLL configuration" and "IP/SYS clock source and clock
  division configuration"
  https://github.com/sophgo/sophgo-doc/blob/main/SG200X/TRM/contents/en/clock/pll_configure.rst
